% A session piped from a CRLF file.  The lexer counts \r as whitespace, so
% queries would parse either way; what breaks without the REPL trimming it
% too is every dot command, which is matched whole -- .quit included, so the
% session would run past the end of what was typed.  The query after .quit
% here is what catches that: its row must not appear.
edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
